    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Kua is one of the largest medieval Swahili sites in East Africa and Stéphane Pradines, Associate Professor, has received an AKU grant to lay the ground work for an archaeological project on Mafia Island and Kua.  Mafia Island  is located at the mouth of the Rufiji River in Tanzania and Kua is on the small island of Juani, to the south-west of Mafia.",
